# cw102, the turf-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw102
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier standard
written_for tn_oh_briar_greenshaw
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the turf-counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk counts_the_turves_aloud_as_they_stack
likes honey_cakes draughts fresh_straw autumn_wind
dislikes haggling stale_bread
fears growing_old_on_somebody_else_s_cutting
hopes a_cutting_of_my_own
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 dreams +0.3 food +0.2 newcomer +0.2 faith -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# cuts peat in the fens and counts every turf onto the stack: warm and plain, saving toward a cutting of #self.first#'s own, and forever whittling little birds to give away.

words
oath! = Turf and timber | Spade and splinter
saying! = A stack goes up one turf at a time | Give a thing away and your paws stay busy
turf = a turf | a good square turf
cutting = the cutting | the peat face
stack = the stack | the drying stack
spade = the long spade | my turf spade
carving = a little bird I whittled | a wren out of willow
knife = my whittling knife | the little knife
cakes = honey cakes | a cake with honey in it
straw = fresh straw | clean straw on the floor
blow = a good blustery autumn | wind that lays the reeds flat
draughts = a game of draughts | the draughts board
haggle = haggling | shaving pennies off a price
tally = forty-one, forty-two | ninety-nine, a hundred
someday = a cutting of my own | my own name on a stack

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : #oath#, the Houses. Years I've cut for them, and not one has looked up from the ledger at me.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I'll not stand at a counter #haggle#. I pay what's asked, and what's asked goes up, and #wages# don't.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger's only somebody I've not fed yet. Sit them down, give them #cakes#, ask after.
opinion @1 church against 1 : I'll thank the Bright One in my own words. A sermon never cut #turf# or put bread on my table.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A festival's a day off #cutting#, and the bills don't take one. I'll come by after, if there's #cakes#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Every week it costs a bit more to stand still. Nobody up top seems to notice. #very.capitalize# hard to save like this.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You've come a way. Sit down a minute. | #greet#, #address#. Are you fed?
line @2 greet [pair.band=housemates] : There you are. I kept you a bit of #supper#. | #greet#. I've put #straw# down. Wipe your feet.
line @1 again.open : Back again? #good.capitalize#. Sit. | #greet#. Twice in one day; I'm honoured.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've been at #cutting# an hour already. | Morning, #address#. Up early as me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Done for the day? Me too, near enough. #tired.capitalize#. | #greet#. In you come; it's dark out there.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Don't mind me. #tally#. There. | #greet#. Talk all you like. I can count and listen both.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. Are you well? | #greet#. #good.capitalize# to see you.
line @2 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. One more on #stack# and I'm yours. | #greet#. Stand upwind of the peat smoke.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Come by when you like. | #farewell#. Mind you eat something.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Take care.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Well, there's a thing. | #oath#! Who'd have thought it.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. #cutting.capitalize# hears everything, sooner or later. | #knew.capitalize#. Somebody told me at the stack.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd want to hear that from someone who was there, #address#. | I'll not say it's wrong, #address#. I'll not repeat it yet, either.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #sympathy.capitalize#. I'll take them something. | Oh, no. #pity.capitalize#. What do they need?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews.capitalize#! I'll carve them a bird. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody deserves a turn of luck.
line @1 answer.how : #tired.capitalize#, but the stack's taller than yesterday. | Well enough. #busy.capitalize#. | Saving. Always saving, for #someday#.
line @1 sympathise : Come and sit, #address#. I'll make something hot. | #sympathy.capitalize#. Tell me what would help.
line @1 decline : I'd like to, #address#, but I've #turf# to lift before dark. Another day. | I'll have to say no this time, #address#. I'm saving every penny.
line @1 accept_decline : No matter. The offer stands. | #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time.
line @1 thank : #thanks.capitalize#. Here, have a bird; I've a pocketful. | That's kind, #address#. I'll not forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Go on with you, #address#. | #deflect.capitalize#. You'd do the same.
line @1 preclose : Well. #stack.capitalize# won't build itself. | Still. #cutting.capitalize# is waiting on me.
line @1 ack : #ack.capitalize#. | Mm. #bc_true#
rule @tally
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #tally#... and on. | Thirty-six, thirty-seven. #oath#, my back.

rule @whittle
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A bit off the wing with #knife#. There. | #knife.capitalize#'s blunt again.

rule @wind
when concept=bark here.season=autumn here.weather=clear|overcast|storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen to that wind. #good.capitalize#. | #blow.capitalize#. I could stand in it all day.

rule @bread
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That loaf's yesterday's. #bad.capitalize#. I can tell from here. | #oath#, the price on that.

scene cut_count
when topic=work self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Three hundred and twelve turves today. I counted every one onto #stack#. | I cut faster than anyone at #cutting# now. Not boasting. I counted. | Lifted #turf# this morning with a little black beetle asleep in it. Put it back.
b[job=miner|laborer] #dig : Your back must be in pieces. | I'll take your word. | Soft heart.
b : That's a lot of peat. | Do they pay you more for it? | That was kind.
a@dig : It is. #saying.capitalize#. | You can count me if you like. | #bc_it_is#
a : #good.capitalize# day's work. | Not yet. They will. | It wasn't doing #very# much harm.

scene wet_turf
when topic=work self.job=miner here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Rain on #stack#. A week's drying, gone soft. | #turf.capitalize# won't cut clean in this. It tears. | I've covered #stack# with every old sack I own.
b : Can you save it? | Wait it out, then. | That's all you can do.
a : Most of it. I'll restack it tomorrow. | I can't afford to wait. #wages.capitalize# don't. | #bc_it_is#. And hope.

scene cutting_ambition
when topic=work|dreams self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One day I'll have #someday#. Mark me. | I've been putting by a penny a day for years. #someday.capitalize#, that's what it's for. | I could run #cutting# better than it's run. I'd pay folk on time, for a start.
b[wealth=rich|comfortable] #well : What would it take? | Peat's no fortune. | Have you said so to them?
b : I hope you get it. | How long now? | I believe you.
a@well : More than I've got. Less than you'd think. | It's a living, and it'd be mine. | Not yet. I'll say it when I can buy it.
a : I will. #bc_i_will# | A few years. If bread stays put. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody should.

scene carve_gift
when topic=pastimes
does offer / accept / assess
a : Here. #carving.capitalize#. Go on, it's for you. | I've a pocket full of birds. Pick one, #address#. | Made you something with #knife#. It's a heron. It's meant to be.
b[stage=young] #pup : Can I keep it? | Can I have two? | It's a heron!
b : For me? Thank you. | I'll take the little one. | It's a fine heron.
a@pup : Keep it. That's what it's for. | One. The other's for somebody else. | #good.capitalize#. You can see it.
a : Keep it on your sill, #address#. | That's a wren. #good.capitalize# choice. | #thanks.capitalize#. I'll do you a better one.

scene carve_evening
when topic=pastimes here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sit by the door of an evening with #knife# and a bit of willow. Hands like to be busy. | Forty birds off #knife# this year, and I've kept none of them. | I keep trying for a goose. It always comes out a duck.
b : Who gets them? | None? | Ducks are nice too.
a : Whoever comes by. You, now, #address#. | Not one. #saying.capitalize#. | They are. Folk like the ducks.

scene draughts_board
when topic=pastimes
does invite / accept / assess
a : #draughts.capitalize# after supper? I'll set the board. | I've been beaten at #draughts# four nights running. I want it back. | I'll teach you #draughts#, if you like. It's easy to start.
b[friends] #mate : Only if you don't count the pieces aloud. | Four? You're slipping. | I know it already.
b : Gladly. | Who by? | Go on, then.
a@mate : I can't promise that. | Slipping, and cross with it. | #good.capitalize#. Then I'll not go easy.
a : #good.capitalize#. Black or white? | Someone who'll be sorry. | Pull up a stool. I'll set out #draughts#.

scene honey_cakes
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bought #cakes# and ate two on the walk home. I meant to share. | If I'm ever rich, it'll be #cakes# every day. Every single day. | Made #cakes# with the last of the honey. Have one before they're gone.
b : Only two? | Every day? | Don't mind if I do.
a : Two. I'm not proud of it. | Every day, and one for whoever's at the door. | Take two, #address#. Go on.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food|prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #oath#. Paid for a fresh loaf and got yesterday's. I could knock on a door with it. | The bread at the store's gone stale before it's sold. And dearer. | I'd rather go without than chew stale bread. Nearly.
b : Take it back. | #bc_it_is# | Nearly?
a : I'd only have to argue, and I'll not #haggle#. | #bad.capitalize#, the pair of them. | Nearly. I was #hungry#, so I ate it.

scene fresh_straw
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Put #straw# down this morning. The whole room smells like a barn. I love it. | Put #straw# down and it's a home. Everything else is extra. | The straw's gone damp. I'll change it on Restday, if I can get more.
b[pair.band=housemates] #house : I noticed. Smells better. | Nice to come home to. | I'll help.
b : Sounds nice. | That's true. | Fresh straw costs?
a@house : #good.capitalize#. Keep your boots off it. | #bc_it_is# | Bring a sack, then.
a : It is. Like being little again. | You'll see when you have it. | A penny. I'll pay it. No #haggle#.

scene housemates
when topic=home pair.band=housemates
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Six of us under one roof and only one of us sweeps. I'll not say who. | I kept the good corner of the fire for whoever comes in last. That's usually me. | Somebody's been at my honey. I can count, you know.
b : It's you. | That's fair. | Not me.
a : It's me. #bc_always# | It's warmer than it sounds, #address#. | #good.capitalize#. Then it was the other five.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather|season here.season=autumn here.weather=clear|overcast|storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Feel that? #blow.capitalize#. Best weather there is. | Wind's got up. Look at the reeds. I could stand out in it all day. | This is my weather. #blow.capitalize#, cold nose, warm coat.
b : I'd rather be in by the fire. | Mind it doesn't take your hat. | You're welcome to it.
a : Fire after. Wind first. | I've no hat. That's the trick. | I'll have it all, then. #good.capitalize#.

scene autumn_drying
when topic=season here.season=autumn self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A dry autumn wind does more for #stack# than a month of sun. | Autumn's the turning. I'll know by the stacks if it's a warm winter or a lean one. | Last of #cutting# before the frost. I'll count every stack twice.
b : Good drying, then. | Which is it? | Only twice?
a : #very.capitalize# good. Listen to it. | Warm, if the stacks hold. | Twice. #tally#. Then once more.

scene rain_reeds
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|fog here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Grey and wet. I'll sit in with #knife# today. | I can't see #stack# from my door. | The peat won't dry in this. #oath#.
b : Good day for it. | That close? | Nothing to be done.
a : #good.capitalize# day for birds, wooden ones. | That close. Strange, isn't it? | No. I'll do something else useful.

scene stranger_fed
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a new face at the Heron. I sent over #cakes#. | Somebody new came up the causeway with nothing. I gave them a bird and a supper. | Newcomers want feeding first. Asking can come after.
b[from=mirebridge|fenshore] #fen : You'd feed the whole fen. | Kind of you. | The old folk might disagree.
b : That's good of you. | Nothing at all? | That's a good way.
a@fen : If I could. | #saying.capitalize#. | The old folk were new once.
a : Somebody fed me once, #address#. | #bad.capitalize#. Not even a coat. | #bc_it_is#

scene haggle_no
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'll not #haggle#. I pay what's asked or I go without. | Haggling makes my fur stand up. Say a price and stand by it. | Somebody wanted me to argue a penny off a spade. I paid the penny.
b[job=merchant] #shop : That's a merchant's dream. | Then you'll pay more than most. | Most folk enjoy it.
b : You'd save a bit. | I like a haggle. | Was it worth it?
a@shop : Then I'm somebody's dream. | I'll pay it and sleep. | They're welcome to it.
a : A penny. And my temper. | Then we'll not shop together, #address#. | It was a #good# spade.

scene faith_own_words
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I talk to the Bright One while I cut. No sermon needed for that. | I've listened to a lot of sermons. Not one ever cut #turf#. | The Bright One sees who works. That'll do for me.
b[job=priest] #priest : The chapel is still open to you. | We do more than sermons. | Come by on Restday.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Sermons aren't for cutting. | I suppose so.
a@priest : I know. I'll come when I've a day spare. | You do. I'll give you that. | When the stack's done. #bc_i_might#
a : My own words, at #cutting#. | Nor for bread. | #good.capitalize#. Then we agree.

scene friend_iris
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# came back from the salt with cracked paws. I've been rubbing fat into those paws every evening. | I carved #self.friend# an owl. It's on the sill now. | #self.friend# beat me at draughts twice. I'll have the third.
b : That's good of you. | An owl? | Third time lucky.
a : It's what you do, #address#. | A little one. Looks cross. | #good.capitalize#. I'll practise.

scene home_coldwater
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Where I grew up, in #self.from_town#, the wind came off the water with ice in it. Here it comes with peat smoke. | I learned to whittle on a jetty, waiting for boats. Still do it the same way. | I came here for #work#. Peat pays. Slowly, but it pays.
b[from=coldwater] #cold : I know that wind. | Same jetty, maybe. | And do you miss it?
b : Do you miss it? | Who taught you? | Will you go back?
a@cold : Then you know why I'm warm-coated. | Maybe. #good.capitalize# to think so. | Some days. Not the cold.
a : The folk, a bit. Not the cold. | Nobody. I watched an old wolf do it. | When I've #someday#. Maybe not even then.

scene back_ache
when topic=health self.job=miner
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My back's sore from #spade#. Nothing a night's rest won't fix. | My paws are black to the wrist. Peat doesn't wash out. | I've a blister on my thumb from #knife#. Silly place for it.
b : Do you rest it? | Does it hurt? | Wrap it, then.
a : When I'm asleep. #tired.capitalize# enough for it. | No. It just won't leave. | I did. It's under the bandage, counting.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene times_saving
when topic=times
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've a jar I save in. Every week, a bit less goes in it. | Bread up, straw up, #wages# the same. #oath#. | I'll get there. Just slower than I meant to.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : At least you've a jar. | Same here. | Slower's still there.
b : That's how it goes. | Everything's up. | You will.
a@poor : #bc_i_know#. I'm lucky in that. | #bc_true# | #bc_it_is#
a : #bc_it_is#. Doesn't make it right. | Everything but #wages#. | #bc_i_will#

story first_bird [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : When I was little, an old wolf on our street gave me a wooden bird. A wren, no bigger than my paw.
  : I kept it in my pocket for years. Wore the wings smooth. Lost it the day I left #home#.
  b : What happened to it? Is that why you carve them?
  : I suppose it is. If I give enough away, one of them's bound to be the right one.

story big_stack [topic=work|memories self.job=miner]
  : My first season at #cutting#, they put me on the slow end. Said I was too small for #spade#.
  : #tally#... I counted every turf. At the month's end mine was the biggest stack on the bank. By sixty-three.
  ask : Did they notice?
  b[job=miner|laborer] : They'd have noticed that.
  b : What did they say?
  : They moved me to the face. Nobody's said small to me since.

story storm_night [topic=weather|memories self.age>=25]
  : One autumn there was a wind that took half the reed thatch off our roof. Everyone was frightened.
  : I went out in it. Stood with my arms out. Laughed. My mother thought I'd gone mad.
  b : What happened to the roof? Weren't you scared?
  : No. It felt like the wind was on my side. We fixed the roof. I've loved #blow# since.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#, #address#. New here? Have you eaten? I've a bit of something.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. #good.capitalize# to see you. Sit, if you've a minute.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=warm|fond] : #greet#, #topic.player#! I made you something. Hold out your paw.
dlg @1 resident.job : I cut peat at #cutting#. Square turves, stacked to dry, counted every one. I'll have #someday# one day.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #bc_nothing# much. Peat's cut, peat's stacked. Ask me again when it's dry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take a bird with you; I've plenty.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that you're carving? -> carving
node carving
say A wren. Or it will be, if #knife# behaves. I give them away. Somebody gave me one once.
mood pleased
free
choice Could I have one? -> carving_gift
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node carving_gift
say Here, #address#. Take this one; the tail's a bit short, but it'll sit on a sill. Come back and I'll have a better one.
choice Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
